      "output": "The spike (AI-3110) is merged and produced `docs/read-only.md`. Let me verify it contains the mapping table and shape decision this ticket depends on.\nThis ticket is exceptionally well-specified and correctly targeted at this repo.\n\n**Verification:**\n- The blocking spike **AI-3110 is merged** (commit `fd4a8ed`) and produced `docs/read-only.md` — a complete per-harness mapping table with exact args for all five harnesses (claude/codex/grok/opencode/pi) and a signed-off shape decision.\n- All files the ticket names exist: `src/approval-mode.ts` (the module to mirror), `src/harnesses.ts`, `src/headless-run.ts`, `src/main.ts`, plus the `createFakeHarness` test pattern in `src/harnesses.test.ts`/`src/headless-run.test.ts`.\n- The spike resolves the two open design questions the implementation would otherwise have to guess: the flag shape (orthogonal boolean, single permission-posture resolution function that suppresses colliding approval args) and the no-mechanism behavior (refuse-to-launch; opencode explicitly reclassified with a mechanism).\n\n**Scope:** Single deliverable — implement `--read-only` for `eh run`. Three behavior-changing ACs (per-harness mapping, never-silently-unrestricted invariant, composition with `defaultApprovalMode: auto`), all facets of one coherent feature that ships as one focused PR mirroring the prior approval-defaults change (#42). Not too broad.\n\n**Specification:** The spike is the spec — exact args, collision behavior, and interaction decisions are all documented. No author-level decisions are left ambiguous.\n\n**Repository:** Correct target — this is the `eh` CLI, the files and the spike all live here.\n\nThis is a clean proceed.\n\nSTATUS:proceed\n",
